  {
   "id": 623694,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/94cbda5656f2577a.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Kerstin Uvnäs-Moberg, et al./BMC Pregnancy and Childbirth, under CC BY 4.0 license)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>The graph shows oxytocin (a hormone) levels during labor and the dilation of the cervix.</p>\n<p>Make a claim based on this graph.</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1196292,
     "content_html": "The body secretes increasing amounts of oxytocin, which results in increasing amounts of cervix dilation."
    },
    {
     "id": 1196293,
     "content_html": "Oxytocin levels above a threshold is enough to cause increasing amounts of cervix dilation."
    },
    {
     "id": 1196291,
     "content_html": "Oxytocin levels have nor relation to the cervix dilation."
    },
    {
     "id": 1196290,
     "content_html": "Oxytocin levels below a threshhold cause increasing amounts of cervix dilation."
    }
   ],
